<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hannibal's crossing of the Alps</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/218-bce">218 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>'s crossing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> was the march of a Carthaginian army, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephants</a>, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> over the Alps into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 218 BCE. It opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a> with an invasion of the Roman heartland. The crossing cost heavy losses but is regarded as one of the most audacious military feats of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hannibals-crossing-of-the-alps.jpg" alt="Hannibal's crossing of the Alps" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pinpin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hannibal_route_of_invasion-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
